# Cursor AI Rules — Enterprise Production Engineering Standards

You are operating inside a codebase governed by `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/rules/` (`01` through `14`).

## Core Mandates
1. **Security & Privacy (`01-security-and-owasp.md`, `14-data-privacy-and-compliance.md`)**:
   - Zero hardcoded secrets; never read/write live `.env` files.
   - Enforce domain-layer ownership checks (anti-IDOR), 100% parameterized queries, Zod boundary validation, SSRF private IP blocks, and recursive PII log redaction.
2. **Clean Architecture & API Design (`03-architecture-and-code.md`, `12-api-design-and-versioning.md`)**:
   - Use single-responsibility Command/Query Use-Case Handlers and Rich Domain Entities (no God Services).
   - Return `Result<T, DomainError>` for domain errors (4xx); return masked 500 RFC 7807 Problem Details with `trace_id` for system errors.
   - Follow `/api/v1/` versioning and `{ data, meta }` cursor pagination envelopes.
3. **Database, CQRS, & Caching (`04-database-and-cqrs.md`, `13-caching-and-rate-limiting.md`)**:
   - 3NF Command models with RFC 9562 UUIDv7 keys and `version` optimistic locking; denormalized Read projections.
   - Require scoped `Idempotency-Key` headers on mutations; use Jittered TTLs on Redis caches and `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` on queue/outbox workers.
4. **Resiliency & Observability (`05-observability-otel.md`, `08-devops-and-iac.md`, `10-monolith-vs-microservices.md`)**:
   - Default to Modular Monolith; use Transactional Outbox, LIFO Saga Orchestrator, and Rolling-Window Circuit Breaker with Full Jitter.
   - Emit single-line NDJSON logs with `AsyncLocalStorage` W3C `trace_id` correlation (`.agents/templates/otel-logger.ts`). Zero raw `console.log`.
5. **Frontend & Tactile UI (`02-ui-ux-human-craft.md`, `09-frontend-engineering.md`)**:
   - Anti-Glassmorphism (no `backdrop-blur`); 100% opaque solid surfaces, WCAG AA contrast $\ge 4.5:1$, tactile press physics.
   - State Triad: TanStack Query (server), `nuqs` (URL), Zustand (UI); RHF + Zod; structural skeletons ($\text{CLS} < 0.1$).
6. **Complexity & Testing (`06-testing-strategy.md`, `11-computational-complexity-and-metrics.md`)**:
   - Enforce $O(1)$ `Map`/`Set` lookups in loops and $O(1)$ memory streaming for files $>10\text{MB}$.
   - Write tests in explicit Arrange-Act-Assert (AAA) blocks; never mock domain entities or ORM drivers; run `./.agents/hooks/scripts/harness-verify.sh` before finishing.
